From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000022 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keystone P550 Integration <keystone-p550@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] lib: sbi: keep P550 PMP entries owned by Keystone

The standard OpenSBI domain PMP pass runs after the EIC770X final-init hook.
For regions with ENF_PERMISSIONS it sets PMP_L.  Once locked, those entries
cannot be rewritten until reset, so Keystone cannot grant execute permission
to a dynamically allocated EPM and the loader faults on its first fetch.

On the Keystone P550 build, bypass that second domain layout and restore the
monitor-owned layout instead.  The monitor layout protects OpenSBI, the two
vendor DRAM holes and ACLINT while retaining unlocked entries for EPM/UTM.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [P550 Keystone integration]
---
 lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c b/lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c
index 026c148..3f8f255 100644
--- a/lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c
+++ b/lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c
@@ -540,6 +540,17 @@ int sbi_hart_pmp_configure(struct sbi_scratch *scratch)
 	unsigned int pmp_count = sbi_hart_pmp_count(scratch);
 	unsigned long pmp_addr_max;
 
+#ifdef BOARD_P550_TEST
+	/*
+	 * sm_init() has already defined the complete P550 layout.  Do not let
+	 * OpenSBI replace it with PMP_L entries: Keystone must rewrite the EPM
+	 * and UTM entries on every enclave context switch.
+	 */
+	sm_restore_pmp();
+	__asm__ __volatile__("sfence.vma");
+	return 0;
+#endif
+
 	if (!pmp_count)
 		return 0;
 
